#
# Build artefacts that must never enter the build context.
#
# native/bin/ holds binaries produced by a developer's local `go build`. The
# go-builder stage compiles its own from source, so shipping these would only
# bust the layer cache on every local build and risk baking a stale binary into
# an image.
#
# __pycache__ directories are written by whichever interpreter ran last; when a
# container writes them through a bind mount they end up owned by root, which
# then blocks a normal `rm` on the host.
native/bin/
native/packaging/dist/
**/__pycache__/
